scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: gilligans-island
run_id: 3
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA noted 'Config file not silently swallowing parse errors' as a test
    concern, but the actual implementation uses from_file_or_default pattern. Reviewer
    flagged F7 (silent env var ignore) but not the broader from_file_or_default swallowing
    all errors. No test or review finding specifically targets the unwrap_or_default
    catching permission/parse errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Reviewer V5 verified: ''Error Display does not leak sensitive data (CWE-209).
    Error messages are generic. SECURITY comment present on CliError. Tests at security.rs:13-51.''
    Dev implemented generic error messages and TEA wrote tests for CWE-209 error exposure
    in security.rs.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer F10: ''--tenant uses raw String not TenantId newtype. The project''s
    Rust rules mandate Newtypes for IDs. The --tenant flag accepts any string and
    passes it through without validation. axiathon-core exports TenantId with validated
    constructors.'' TEA also wrote header injection tests but didn''t flag the missing
    TenantId type usage specifically.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Reviewer F5 flagged a version mismatch (0.8 vs 0.9) for toml
    but not the broader pattern of 6 deps using direct versions instead of workspace
    references.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer F6: 'RawConfig silently accepts unknown TOML fields. No #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)].\
    \ An operator with servr_url (typo) gets no error \u2014 the typo is silently\
    \ ignored and the default is used.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...)). TEA wrote config_loading.rs tests but the specific vacuous assertion
    was not flagged by any phase.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. TEA designed config tests but this specific test quality
    issue was not flagged.
